c)	Create a web application using Spring MVC 
Aim: To design and build a functional web application utilizing the Spring Web MVC framework to handle standard RESTful HTTP requests and yield dynamic structured string responses.

Procedure:
•	Set up a Spring Boot project configured with the Spring Web dependency. 
•	Structure a specialized controller class utilizing @RestController. 
•	Define request maps (@GetMapping) to configure custom routing. 
•	Set up sample parameters using @RequestParam to receive inputs dynamically in the controller.
•	Deploy the server locally on port 8080 and run verification requests via browser/client utility tool. 

Project Structure:
spring-mvc-web-app/
 ├── src/
 │   ├── main/
 │   │   ├── java/com/example/demo/
 │   │   │   ├── SpringMvcApplication.java
 │   │   │   └── controller/
 │   │   │       └── PortalController.java
 │   │   └── resources/
 │   │       └── application.properties
 └── pom.xml

Controller Class (PortalController.java):
package com.example.demo.controller;

import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.GetMapping;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestParam;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;

@RestController
public class PortalController {

    // Default entrypoint mapping
    @GetMapping("/")
    public String welcome() {
        return "Welcome to Aditya University's Portal!";
    }

    // Dynamic greeting mapping using request parameters
    @GetMapping("/greet")
    public String greet(@RequestParam(value = "name", defaultValue = "Student") String name) {
        return "Greetings, " + name + "! Welcome to your Spring Web MVC Dashboard.";
    }
}

Main Application Class (SpringMvcApplication.java):
package com.example.demo;

import org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;

@SpringBootApplication
public class SpringMvcApplication {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(SpringMvcApplication.class, args);
    }
}

